 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Articles in the genitive",
     "texto": [
      "With masculine and neuter: **des** (of the): **des Vaters** (of the father), **des Hauses** (of the house). With feminine: **der** (of the): **der Frau** (of the woman). In plural: **der** (of the): **der Kinder** (of the children).",
      "Masculine and neuter nouns add **-s** or **-es**: **des Mannes**, **des Kindes**. Watch out: the feminine and the plural do not change the form of the noun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Possession with the genitive",
     "texto": [
      "The possessed noun is placed first and the possessor afterwards in the genitive: **Das Auto meines Freundes** (my friend's car). In everyday speech one more often says **das Auto von meinem Freund** (with «von» and the dative), but the genitive is more formal and very frequent in texts."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Weak masculines",
     "texto": [
      "Some masculine nouns add **-(e)n** in almost all cases: **der Kollege, den Kollegen, dem Kollegen, des Kollegen**. The same happens with **der Kunde** and **der Student**. Learn these forms together with the article; not all masculines follow this pattern."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
